---

<DocsLayout
  title="Key Management"
  description="Key generation, Ed25519 vs ES256 comparison, low-level crypto utilities, and security guidance for the Attestto VC SDK."
  currentPath="/docs/credentials/key-management/"
  structuredData={structuredData}
>
  <h1>Key Management</h1>
  <p class="docs-hero-sub">
    Generate key pairs, choose the right algorithm, and handle keys securely.
    All cryptography is pure JavaScript via <code>@noble/curves</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>generateKeyPair()</h2>
  <p>The primary key generation function:</p>

  <CodeBlock lang="TypeScript" title="Generate Ed25519 keys (default)">
<Fragment set:html={`<span class="c-kw">import</span> <span class="c-br">{</span> generateKeyPair <span class="c-br">}</span> <span class="c-kw">from</span> <span class="c-str">'@attestto-com/vc-sdk'</span>

<span class="c-cm">// Ed25519 (default — recommended)</span>
<span class="c-kw">const</span> ed25519Keys = <span class="c-fn">generateKeyPair</span>()

<span class="c-cm">// ES256 (ECDSA over P-256)</span>
<span class="c-kw">const</span> es256Keys = <span class="c-fn">generateKeyPair</span>(<span class="c-str">'ES256'</span>)`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <h2>KeyPair interface</h2>

  <CodeBlock lang="TypeScript" title="KeyPair interface">
<Fragment set:html={`<span class="c-kw">interface</span> <span class="c-typ">KeyPair</span> <span class="c-br">{</span>
  algorithm: <span class="c-str">'Ed25519'</span> <span class="c-op">|</span> <span class="c-str">'ES256'</span>
  publicKey: <span class="c-typ">Uint8Array</span>
  privateKey: <span class="c-typ">Uint8Array</span>
<span class="c-br">}</span>`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <h2>Ed25519 vs ES256</h2>

  <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.9rem; margin: 1.5rem 0;">
    <thead>
      <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--docs-border, #333);">
        <th style="text-align: left; padding: 0.75rem; color: var(--docs-text);">Property</th>
        <th style="text-align: left; padding: 0.75rem; color: var(--docs-text);">Ed25519</th>
        <th style="text-align: left; padding: 0.75rem; color: var(--docs-text);">ES256</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody style="color: var(--docs-text-muted);">
      <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--docs-border, #333);">
        <td style="padding: 0.75rem;">Curve</td>
        <td style="padding: 0.75rem;">Curve25519</td>
        <td style="padding: 0.75rem;">P-256 (secp256r1)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--docs-border, #333);">
        <td style="padding: 0.75rem;">Signature type</td>
        <td style="padding: 0.75rem;">EdDSA</td>
        <td style="padding: 0.75rem;">ECDSA</td>
      </tr>
      <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--docs-border, #333);">
        <td style="padding: 0.75rem;">Key size</td>
        <td style="padding: 0.75rem;">32 bytes</td>
        <td style="padding: 0.75rem;">32 bytes (private), 65 bytes (public)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--docs-border, #333);">
        <td style="padding: 0.75rem;">Signature size</td>
        <td style="padding: 0.75rem;">64 bytes</td>
        <td style="padding: 0.75rem;">64 bytes</td>
      </tr>
      <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--docs-border, #333);">
        <td style="padding: 0.75rem;">Performance</td>
        <td style="padding: 0.75rem;">Faster signing and verification</td>
        <td style="padding: 0.75rem;">Slower, but still fast in pure JS</td>
      </tr>
      <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--docs-border, #333);">
        <td style="padding: 0.75rem;">Hardware support</td>
        <td style="padding: 0.75rem;">Limited HSM support</td>
        <td style="padding: 0.75rem;">Broad HSM/TPM support</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td style="padding: 0.75rem;">Recommendation</td>
        <td style="padding: 0.75rem;"><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">Default choice</strong></td>
        <td style="padding: 0.75rem;">Use when HSM/WebAuthn compat needed</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Low-level crypto utilities</h2>
  <p>The SDK exports utilities for direct cryptographic operations:</p>

  <CodeBlock lang="TypeScript" title="sign() and verify()">
<Fragment set:html={`<span class="c-kw">import</span> <span class="c-br">{</span> sign, verify <span class="c-br">}</span> <span class="c-kw">from</span> <span class="c-str">'@attestto-com/vc-sdk'</span>

<span class="c-kw">const</span> message = <span class="c-kw">new</span> <span class="c-fn">TextEncoder</span>().<span class="c-fn">encode</span>(<span class="c-str">'Hello, world'</span>)

<span class="c-cm">// Sign a message</span>
<span class="c-kw">const</span> signature = <span class="c-fn">sign</span>(message, keys.privateKey, <span class="c-str">'Ed25519'</span>)

<span class="c-cm">// Verify a signature</span>
<span class="c-kw">const</span> isValid = <span class="c-fn">verify</span>(message, signature, keys.publicKey, <span class="c-str">'Ed25519'</span>)
console.<span class="c-fn">log</span>(isValid) <span class="c-cm">// true</span>`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <CodeBlock lang="TypeScript" title="Encoding utilities">
<Fragment set:html={`<span class="c-kw">import</span> <span class="c-br">{</span> toBase64url, fromBase64url, toHex <span class="c-br">}</span> <span class="c-kw">from</span> <span class="c-str">'@attestto-com/vc-sdk'</span>

<span class="c-cm">// Encode a public key for storage or transport</span>
<span class="c-kw">const</span> encoded = <span class="c-fn">toBase64url</span>(keys.publicKey)
console.<span class="c-fn">log</span>(encoded) <span class="c-cm">// 'dGhpcyBpcyBhIHB1YmxpYyBrZXk...'</span>

<span class="c-cm">// Decode back to Uint8Array</span>
<span class="c-kw">const</span> decoded = <span class="c-fn">fromBase64url</span>(encoded)

<span class="c-cm">// Hex encoding for debugging</span>
<span class="c-kw">const</span> hex = <span class="c-fn">toHex</span>(keys.publicKey)
console.<span class="c-fn">log</span>(hex) <span class="c-cm">// '7468697320697320612...'</span>`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <h2>Security guidance</h2>

  <Callout type="warning">
    <strong>Never expose private keys in frontend code.</strong> Private keys should only
    exist server-side or in secure enclaves (wallets, HSMs, TEEs). Use
    <code>verifyWithKey</code> on the client with the <em>public</em> key only.
  </Callout>

  <ul style="color: var(--docs-text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 2; padding-left: 1.5rem;">
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">Server-side issuance</strong> — run <code>VCIssuer</code> on your backend. Never ship private keys to the browser.</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">Environment variables</strong> — store keys in <code>process.env</code> or a secrets manager, not in source code.</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">Key rotation</strong> — use the <code>keyId</code> field to version your keys. Old credentials remain verifiable with old public keys.</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">Wallet delegation</strong> — for user-held keys, let a wallet (Attestto ID, browser extension) manage the private key. Your app never touches it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Next steps</h2>
  <ul style="color: var(--docs-text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 2; padding-left: 1.5rem;">
    <li><a href="/docs/credentials/issuing/">Issuing credentials</a> — use keys with VCIssuer</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/credentials/verifying/">Verifying credentials</a> — use public keys for verification</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/credentials/schemas/">Schemas &amp; plugins</a> — add domain-specific types</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
